# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — host-agnostic, applied AFTER Pages Functions
# (middleware) on both premiselabs.co and tortoise.premiselabs.co.
#
# 1) Trailing-slash variants: Cloudflare Pages serves a built-in 308
#    clean-URL redirect to the extensionless form; these explicit 301s
#    standardize the status code and target so every host/path variant
#    resolves identically to the canonical URL.
# 2) /index.html is the raw asset behind BOTH host roots — 301 to "/" so the
#    middleware root rewrite (company page / product page) owns the URL.
# 3) AUTH CONSOLIDATION: there is ONE auth page — /auth (served from the
#    signup.html asset via a 200 rewrite). The legacy /signup and /signin
#    URLs (and their .html / trailing-slash variants) 301 to /auth so the
#    whole funnel (login buttons, dashboard/welcome redirects, OAuth +
#    recovery links, marketing CTAs) converges on a single screen. The 200
#    rewrite is terminal — the target asset is served without re-evaluating
#    redirect rules.

# /auth is served by the middleware (functions/_middleware.ts — it owns
# the URL on every host, rewriting to the /signup asset). /signup and its
# variants stay a redirect-free legacy alias of the same page (clean-URL
# resolution serves signup.html; the canonical tag points at /auth, so SEO
# consolidates). /signin and its variants 301 to /auth — the old standalone
# login screen is gone. Trailing-slash variants are pinned 301s (the file's
# standardization contract; Pages' built-in 308s are not relied on):
/auth/   /auth  301
/signup/  /signup  301
/signin   /auth  301
/signin/  /auth  301
/signin.html  /auth  301

# Trailing-slash → canonical
/privacy/  /privacy  301
/tos/      /tos      301
/license/  /license  301
/dpa/      /dpa      301
/security/ /security 301
/aviso-privacidad/  /aviso-privacidad  301
/docs/     /docs     301
/self-hosted/  /self-hosted  301
/welcome/  /welcome  301
/invite-accept/  /invite-accept  301

# Raw index asset → host root (middleware rewrites / per host)
/index.html  /  301

# .html extension duplicates (non-auth only)
/docs.html  /docs          301
/self-hosted.html  /self-hosted  301
